  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1034 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nThe other thing that the next few days will bring us is much drier \nconditions. This will give our soils an opportunity to recover, \nwhich several areas in the mid-state need before rains return. \nSpeaking of, that next chance of rain will rear its head on \nSaturday. Yes, just in time for the weekend, an upper level low will \ndig out of the northern Plains and into the TN/Ohio Valleys. Models \naren't handling the arrival of said rain very well. Some have \narrival Friday night and other hold off until Saturday morning. \nWe'll work out those details over the next couple of days. Either \nway, there's a medium to high chance Saturday and Sunday will be \nwet. While I'm still not seeing a signal for severe weather, there \nhas been talk about excessive rainfall this weekend. Now, I'm not \npoo-pooing the idea completely. However, looking at NBM probs over \nthe last few runs, the likelihood of seeing more than 1.5 inches \nstands at about 15%. This is where the recovery time through the \nrest of the workweek may come into play. We'll fine tune this over \nthe next couple of days, but for now, we can expect temperatures at \nor just below normal and a wet weekend to come.",
